            0.559
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Notations"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.57,
            0.848,
            0.645
          ],
          "content": "In mathematics, we use an arrow mark (>) to show that a set of lines is parallel. If there is more than one set of parallel lines (as in Fig. 5. 9), the second set is shown with two arrow marks and so on. Perpendicular lines are marked with a square angle between them."
